## Actions
Reviewed the existing CoreWeave data sources, shared HTTP client, provider registration, generated documentation workflow, acceptance-test routing, and relevant public pull request reviews. Added coreweave_caller_identity, a two-field response model, an authenticated read through the shared retrying HTTP client, provider registration, a protocol-level fake-server test, a dedicated read-only acceptance suite, a minimal example, and generated documentation. Removed response fields outside the public data source contract from the test fixture. Ran the focused test, suite sweep, live suite target, full test suite, lint, build, documentation generation, module tidy diff, and diff check.

## Errors & Mistakes
The first documentation-generation run during the final audit could not start the locally built provider inside the process sandbox and reported "Unrecognized remote plugin message". The same command passed with normal process permissions. The first public commit metadata included local validation paths and research details that were not part of the public contract; the commit message and notes reference were rewritten during the public audit. The first live acceptance test was in the root Go package, which the repository acceptance matrix does not schedule. The final CI audit found this gap, so the data source and tests moved into a caller_identity package and that suite was added to both acceptance-test lists. The first public CI rerun also repeated unrelated failures in CKS cleanup, inference prerequisites, and object-storage convergence.

## Dead Ends
No existing provider dependency exposes this identity route. Adding a new schema dependency was unnecessary for a two-field read, so the implementation uses the authenticated JSON endpoint and the provider's existing HTTP client. Leaving the live test in the root package would have made it manual-only, so the data source uses a suite-shaped package even though it has no resources to sweep. Additional identity attributes were excluded because the requested public contract contains only organization_id and user_id.

## Hints for Future Agents
The JSON response maps principal.orgUid to organization_id and principal.uid to user_id. Connect interceptors do not apply to the direct JSON request, so the request must attach the configured bearer token and user agent. Keep the schema at two computed attributes unless the public product contract expands. Update both the make suite list and workflow suite list when renaming or removing the acceptance package.

## Codebase Discoveries
Data sources are registered by the provider's DataSources method. Documentation is generated from examples and provider schemas with make generate. The shared retryable HTTP client supplies the existing timeout and retry behavior to the identity request. Acceptance suites are selected independently by GNUmakefile and the pull request workflow; root-package acceptance tests are not included.

